# large binary media dropped in by the marketing team
public/media/*.mp4
public/media/*.webm
public/media/*.mov
!public/media/.gitkeep
!public/media/README.md
# The hero background is the exception, and it has to be.
#
# Railway clones the repository fresh on every deploy — there is no persistent
# disk and no upload step — so a file that is only on somebody's laptop is a file
# production never sees. Ignored, the homepage would quietly fall back to the
# vector city scene on the live site while looking correct locally, which is the
# worst kind of difference between the two.
#
# Kept under 4 MB for that reason. Anything genuinely large belongs on a CDN with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_HERO_VIDEO_URL pointing at it — see public/media/README.md.
!public/media/hero.mp4
# And the VP9 copy alongside it. Not for size — on this footage VP9 and H.264
# land within 30 KB of each other — but for coverage: Chromium built from source
# and Firefox on Linux without system codecs cannot decode H.264 at all, and
# would fall back to the vector scene while every other browser showed video.
# `resolveHeroVideo` offers this one first; Safari takes the MP4.
!public/media/hero.webm

